                "text": "**Analyzing Grid Requirements**\n\nOkay, I'm starting to get a grip on this. It seems the problem involves a 1D grid and figuring out how it translates into rows. It seems the output rows depend on the total grid length and the number of non-zero starting elements. For the given example, a grid of length 6 with 3 non-zeros, yields 3 rows. The number of non-zeros in each row seems to increment. Let me explore this pattern further.\n\n\n",
