                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the examples reveals the following rule:\n\n1. Let $W$ be the width of the input row and $k$ be the initial number of colored (non-zero) cells.\n2. The output grid has width $W$ and height $H = W / 2$.\n3. Row $r$ (from $0$ to $H - 1$) starts with $k + r$ cells of the input color, followed by $0$s for the remainder of the row.\n\nI am ready for the test inputs.",
